        "We made it to the trailhead around 10:30 am on Thursday, February 6 of 2014 after a long drive up the mountain (again, many thanks again to Larry and Sharlene). About midway up the winding dirt road, we passed a group of Army Rangers. The silence of hiking over the last few days was interrupted by the occasional sounds of rifle fire as they trained in the hills nearby.",
        "We dropped packs at the trailhead and hiked a mile back to the summit of Springer Mountain where the Appalachian Trail officially begins. We didn't stay long since there wasn't much of a view and had to keep moving to stay on schedule. We hustled back to our packs and were soon on our way towards Maine. The entire path was glazed over with ice. Every branch, every leaf, every weed had grown small white thorns, and the cold winter air created a light blue ambiance around the trail. It was stunning, and the cool temperatures were perfect for keeping a brisk pace without breaking a sweat.",
