        "Crawling into my bivy, I removed all my layers. I slept surprisingly warm even though the wind picked up and it began to snow overnight. By the time I awoke the next morning, there was a light dusting on the ground and the temperatures were below freezing. I've always hated getting up when it's cold, especially when I'm outside and have to pack everything up before hiking. I suppose a big part of hiking 2,000 miles will be suffering through things I don't want to do.",
