        'My hike was going well until I reached the base of Blood Mountain when a serious case of chaffing in my crotch began to impede my progress. Combined with the long, steep uphill to my campsite, I was left both exhausted and in excruciating pain by the time I reached the "shelter" at the top. The site included a composting privy, an abandoned ranger station that was nothing more than concrete floors and stone walls, and fantastic views. I threw my pack down and set arranged my sleeping bag upon my ground pad before headed outside to make some potatoes for dinner and enjoy the sunset.',
        "Exhausted, I headed to bed early. The night was sleepless, maybe totaling four hours of rest. Not long after lying down, I heard something moving outside the shelter. I froze.\nBear? A crazy person?",
